00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:06,540
Conversation 1 Thanks for inviting me out tonight.

2
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:09,180
I've been wanting to try this place for weeks.

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,660
I usually pass it on my way home from work, but never seem to have time to stop.

4
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,060
I've been dying to come here as well.

5
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:22,120
I was worried that the menu might not be accommodating, but one my close friends ate

6
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:22,980
here last week.

7
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:24,280
She's a vegetarian.

8
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:29,240
She told me that there were a lot of options for her, and they offered alternative

9
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:32,480
dishes. But you're not vegetarian, are you?

10
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,100
Well, not entirely.

11
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:39,940
I don't eat meat at all, but I don't have a problem eating fish, seafood, or eggs.

12
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,840
Isn't that very difficult?

13
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:46,640
I can't imagine giving up a premium juicy steak or bacon cheeseburgers.

14
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:47,840
I wouldn't know.

15
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:50,060
My parents followed the same diet.

16
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:55,260
Even when I was younger, we never had meat during meals, and I never really had a

17
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:56,920
craving to try it.

18
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,160
I bet it would be hard, though, giving up something you're accustomed to eating.

19
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:05,300
I tried cutting back on coffee in the morning, and it was awful.

20
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:10,480
Come to think of it, it was probably even worse for my colleagues that had to deal

21
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,940
with me at morning meetings.

22
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:13,980
That's even harder to imagine.

23
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:15,880
You without coffee.

24
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:20,220
So you say your parents also followed a partially vegetarian diet?

25
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,400
Why did they decide to do that?

26
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,320
That's an interesting question.

27
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,380
I never thought to ask them, though.

28
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:29,320
My best guess is for health reasons.

29
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:34,840
They're not terribly active or knowledgeable about animal preservation efforts, but

30
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:36,380
they're serious about their health.

31
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,940
Both are in their 70s now, but eat organic as often as possible and take part in

32
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,060
regular physical exercise.

33
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:48,260
Neither of them has any health problems, and they hardly ever get sick.

34
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,960
In that case, I might give it a try someday.

35
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,000
Now back to the menu.

36
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,360
What are you going to have?

