00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:05,000
Athletes are seen as heroes because they can do things that most of us can't do.

84
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:12,040
They can hit fastballs coming at at nearly 100 miles an hour and leap and hang in

85
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:15,220
the air, seemingly defying gravity.

86
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:21,000
They get paid millions of dollars for their efforts, and their names and faces

87
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,200
appear on everything from running shoes to advertising boards.

88
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:32,260
Athletes who are champions also show qualities such as perseverance, dedication, and

89
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:34,480
the ability to keep their cool under pressure.

90
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:39,400
Many show those same qualities off the playing field, too.

91
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:45,020
Stories about superstar athletes teach us about working hard and believing in

92
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:48,360
ourselves and in being passionate about what we do.

93
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:54,220
Although it's usually bad behavior that gets an athlete a spot on the o 'clock news,

94
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:59,080
many high -profile players work hard to be positive role models to children.

95
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:05,200
They raise money for charities and act as mentors, talking to student groups and

96
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:10,620
volunteering their time to programs that help children keep off drugs and stay in

97
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:15,460
school. Still, even the greatest champions have flaws.

98
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:20,480
Just because an athlete has the perfect golf swing doesn't mean he is the perfect

99
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,940
parent, friend, or spokesperson.

100
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:26,140
They also make mistakes.

101
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:31,100
Separating an athlete's professional and personal lives can be tough.

102
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:36,300
When a sports star gets in trouble with the law or does something wrong in their

103
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:39,720
private life, fans are often left disappointed.

104
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:45,840
Before he died, baseball star Mickey Mantle, who was plagued with alcohol problems,

105
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:50,940
told young ballplayers and the fans who admired him to play like me.

106
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,820
Don't be like me.

