00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:31,740
Recording 1. It has long been scientifically established that weather changes can

139
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,460
affect people's moods.

140
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:39,200
Now a new study has provided evidence that temperature can influence people's

141
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:46,340
personalities. This study of over 1.6 million people revealed that 22 degrees

142
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:49,740
Celsius is the perfect air temperature to live in.

143
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:55,860
city with an average annual temperature closer to 22 tends to have a population who

144
00:09:55,860 --> 00:10:00,860
are agreeable, conscientious, emotionally stable, and outgoing.

145
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:05,800
It is the least taxing temperature for the body to regulate its own temperature.

146
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:11,580
The study was observational and didn't show cause and effect, but the scientists

147
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:16,940
behind it theorize that better weather leads people to leave their home more often.

148
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:22,620
This, in turn, leads to more social interaction, which encourages them to develop a

149
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,540
friendlier and socially more acceptable personality.

150
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:30,400
Warmer climates also make people feel more positive in general.

151
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:34,280
They tend to be more agreeable and conscientious.

152
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:39,860
The findings might help explain why colder and warmer countries tend to produce

153
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:41,800
people with different personalities.

154
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:50,120
Roughly speaking, about 40 of a person's is determined by their genes, the other 60

155
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:51,860
by their environment.

156
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:58,180
It was already well known that personality traits vary across geographic regions.

157
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:04,760
Scientists also knew that these geographic personality traits are associated with a

158
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,840
broad range of consequential outcomes.

159
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:13,460
These outcomes include economic activity, for example, entrepreneurial startup

160
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:18,820
rates, and also crime rates, health behaviors, and health outcomes.

161
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:24,300
And it is well established that personality traits differ between countries.

162
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:28,720
The research team speculated the two might be linked.

163
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:38,660
To test this, they gave online personality tests to 5,587 Chinese students and 1.66

164
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:43,220
million Americans. They then compared the results with the average annual

165
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,120
temperature where they grew up.

166
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:50,000
The tests measured personality along five well -studied characteristics.

167
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:56,560
The five were agreeability, conscientiousness, emotional stability,

168
00:11:57,280 --> 00:12:00,200
outgoingness, and openness to new experiences.

169
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:06,780
In both groups, the researchers found the closer a town's average annual temperature

170
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:12,180
was to 22 degrees, the more its population exhibited those personality

171
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:18,520
characteristics. However, the findings were much stronger for the Chinese group than

172
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,160
the Americans studied,

173
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:25,880
which suggests that though temperature plays a role, it does not play a dominant

174
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,580
role. The effects are fairly weak.

175
00:12:29,060 --> 00:12:33,380
It's unlikely to lead to many arguments over the temperature setting of the office

176
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:39,200
air conditioner. Question 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.

