00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:02,860
Recording 2. Today we're talking about loneliness.

181
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:09,400
Loneliness and social isolation are growing public health concerns for people of all

182
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:13,580
ages in the United States, from adolescents to the elderly.

183
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:18,820
Public health experts are worried because loneliness seems to be on the rise, and

184
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:24,460
studies have long found correlations between loneliness and an assortment of medical

185
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:27,260
conditions that threaten health and longevity.

186
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:32,060
The problem of loneliness may be even greater than we thought.

187
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:37,740
A new national poll found that about a third of older Americans are lonely, and

188
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:40,080
almost as seniors feel isolated.

189
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:46,000
This is a serious problem as research shows that chronic loneliness is particularly

190
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,860
harmful to senior citizens.

191
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:53,360
That's because it can impair older adults' memory and damage their physical and

192
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:59,300
mental health. Chronic loneliness even impacts the life expectancy of seniors,

193
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:02,640
increasing their risk of early mortality.

194
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,600
Let's take a closer look at that poll now.

195
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:12,540
More than a third of seniors in the poll said they felt lonely at least some of the

196
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:17,600
time, and 27 said they sometimes or often felt isolated.

197
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:22,300
This reflects how much time the seniors spent with others.

198
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:29,360
Almost 30 said they socialized with friends, family, or neighbors once a week or

199
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:34,160
less. Women were more likely than men to report loneliness.

200
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,840
But there is good news.

201
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:41,660
It looks like loneliness can be reversed, but researchers are still trying to

202
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:43,580
determine the best way to do so.

203
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,300
Why is that?

204
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:50,640
Resolving the problem of loneliness among seniors often isn't as simple as getting

205
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:54,260
them together with others or moving them in with their children.

206
00:14:55,040 --> 00:15:00,060
In fact, the poll found that seniors who lived with their children were more likely

207
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:02,920
to report feeling lonely than those who didn't.

208
00:15:03,900 --> 00:15:09,540
This may be because loneliness refers to the discrepancy between actual and desired

209
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:15,700
relationships. So it's possible that someone who lives alone doesn't meet that

210
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:20,220
definition, while someone in a house full of busy people does.

211
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:22,980
How can we solve the problem?

212
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:29,240
Well, the researchers assert that it's important to address each person's underlying

213
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:36,340
cause of loneliness, whether it's the death of a spouse, medical problems, or social

214
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,960
expectations that haven't been fulfilled.

215
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:43,600
It's noteworthy that there is one general recommendation.

216
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:47,680
While finding solutions for loneliness is highly personal,

217
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:53,380
research suggests the best interventions are those that involve meaningful social

218
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:56,260
contact at least once a week.

219
00:15:56,260 --> 00:16:01,860
Depending on the person, that could mean volunteering, seeing an old friend, or

220
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:08,920
something else. Questions 19 to 21 are based on the recording you have just heard.

221
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:15,920
Question 19. Why does the speaker say the finding of a new national poll reveals a

222
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:19,260
serious problem? Question 20.

